<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kanongesha</h1><p class="st-meta">1720 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ndembu Lunda chiefdom of the upper Zambezi watershed, an outpost of Lunda kingship later made famous by anthropological studies of its rituals.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kanongesha title was established in the 18th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> nobles who moved south-west from the court of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a> into the headwaters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabompo-river">Kabompo</a> rivers. They settled among local peoples who became known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndembu-people">Ndembu</a> or Southern Lunda.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Kanongesha held senior rank over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndembu-people">Ndembu</a> sub-chiefs, but his power was limited and largely ritual, rooted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> titles, perpetual kinship between offices, and ties to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwata-yamvo">Mwata Yamvo</a>. Villages farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassava">cassava</a> and hunted, and in the 19th century the area supplied slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and beeswax to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovimbundu">Ovimbundu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chokwe">Chokwe</a> traders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Colonial boundaries drawn in the early 20th century divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndembu-people">Ndembu</a> between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-angola">Portuguese Angola</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belgian-congo">Belgian Congo</a>. The chieftaincy continues in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-turner">Victor Turner's</a> studies of Ndembu ritual in the 1950s made it well known.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1720 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.93%;width:3.70%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1720 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Lunda religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lunda (Ndembu)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/zambia">Zambia</a>, <a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a>, <a href="/countries/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kanongesha, Ndembu Lunda, Southern Lunda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1813&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kanongesha" aria-label="Kingdom of Kanongesha on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5398 2727 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kanongesha lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5662 2807h0M5720 3066h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5718 2983h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5718 2983h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Zambia. <a href="/atlas?year=1813&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kanongesha">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
